5. Multidimensional Extension and Order Structure

5.1. Operator Hierarchy

· Nominal: \Theta_A(\lambda)
· Robust: \Theta_A^{\mathrm{rob}}(\lambda, \varepsilon) — Section 7
· Learning: \Theta_A^{\mathrm{learn}}(\lambda, n) — Section 8
· Autonomy-constrained: \Theta_A^{\mathrm{auto}}(\lambda, k) — Section 8

5.2. Product Order

Definition 5.1. For x, y \in \mathbb{R}^5:

x \preceq y \iff x_i \leq y_i \ \forall i.

5.3. Order-Embedding Impossibility

Theorem 5.1 (No scalar order embedding). There is no function f: \mathbb{R}^5 \to \mathbb{R} that is simultaneously injective, order-preserving, and order-reflecting.

Proof. Suppose such f exists. Since \mathbb{R} is totally ordered, for any x, y \in \mathbb{R}^5, either f(x) \leq f(y) or f(y) \leq f(x). By order-reflection, either x \preceq y or y \preceq x. But the product order on \mathbb{R}^5 has incomparable pairs, e.g., x = (1,0,0,0,0), y = (0,1,0,0,0). Contradiction. \square

Corollary 5.1. Scalarization is a normative choice, not a discovery.

5.4. Stochastic Dominance Preorder

Definition 5.2. For two agents A, B evaluated against the same reference:

A \succeq_{\mathrm{SD}} B \iff \Theta_A(\lambda) \geq \Theta_B(\lambda) \ \forall \lambda.

Proposition 5.1. \succeq_{\mathrm{SD}} is a preorder, becoming a partial order on the quotient by \sim, where A \sim B iff \Theta_A = \Theta_B.

