Appendix I — Additional Technical Results

I.1. Dominance Quantile Function

Definition I.1. For \theta \in (0,1]:

Q_A(\theta) = \sup\{\lambda : \Theta_A(\lambda) \geq \theta\}.

Proposition I.1 (Duality). Q_A(\theta) \geq \lambda \iff \Theta_A(\lambda) \geq \theta.

Proof. (\Rightarrow) If Q_A(\theta) \geq \lambda, then there exists \lambda' \geq \lambda with \Theta_A(\lambda') \geq \theta. Since \Theta_A is non-increasing, \Theta_A(\lambda) \geq \Theta_A(\lambda') \geq \theta.

(\Leftarrow) If \Theta_A(\lambda) \geq \theta, then \lambda \in \{\lambda' : \Theta_A(\lambda') \geq \theta\}, so Q_A(\theta) = \sup\{\cdots\} \geq \lambda. \square

Proposition I.2. Q_A is non-increasing and right-continuous.

Proof. Standard properties of generalized inverses of monotone functions. \square

---

I.2. Interpolation of the Dominance Region

Definition I.2. The Pareto frontier of \mathcal{D}_A is

\operatorname{Pareto}(\mathcal{D}_A) = \left\{(\lambda, \theta) \in \mathcal{D}_A : \nexists (\lambda', \theta') \in \mathcal{D}_A, (\lambda, \theta) \prec (\lambda', \theta')\right\}.

Proposition I.3. Under the product order on \mathbb{R}^2, \operatorname{Pareto}(\mathcal{D}_A) = \{(\lambda, \Theta_A(\lambda)) : \lambda \in \mathbb{R}\} \cap \mathcal{D}_A.

Proof. For each \lambda, the maximal \theta such that (\lambda, \theta) \in \mathcal{D}_A is \Theta_A(\lambda). The point (\lambda, \Theta_A(\lambda)) is Pareto-optimal if there is no \lambda' > \lambda with \Theta_A(\lambda') > \Theta_A(\lambda), which is true when \Theta_A is strictly decreasing. When \Theta_A is constant on an interval, only the right endpoint is Pareto-optimal. \square

---

I.3. The Area Under the Dominance Survival Function

Definition I.3.

\mathrm{AUC}_A = \int_{\mathbb{R}} \Theta_A(\lambda) \, d\lambda.

Proposition I.4. If X_A \in [-1, 1] almost surely, then \mathrm{AUC}_A = \mathbb{E}[X_A] + 1.

Proof. By Fubini's theorem,

\int_{-\infty}^{\infty} \Theta_A(\lambda) \, d\lambda = \int_{-\infty}^{\infty} \Pr(X_A \geq \lambda) \, d\lambda = \int_{-\infty}^{\infty} \mathbb{E}[\mathbf{1}_{\{X_A \geq \lambda\}}] \, d\lambda = \mathbb{E}\left[\int_{-\infty}^{X_A} d\lambda\right] = \mathbb{E}[X_A + 1].

\square

Remark I.1. The AUC is the mean margin. It is a scalar summary of \Theta_A, and thus loses the structural information of the full survival function.

---

I.4. Numerical Approximation of \Theta_A

Algorithm I.1 (Empirical dominance survival function).

Input: Samples X_{A,1}, \ldots, X_{A,n}; grid \lambda_1 < \cdots < \lambda_m.

Output: \widehat{\Theta}_A(\lambda_j) for j = 1, \ldots, m.

Procedure:

1. Sort the samples: X_{(1)} \leq \cdots \leq X_{(n)}.
2. For each j, compute \widehat{\Theta}_A(\lambda_j) = \frac{1}{n} \sum_i \mathbf{1}_{\{X_i \geq \lambda_j\}}.
3. Return the vector (\widehat{\Theta}_A(\lambda_j))_{j=1}^m.

Complexity: O(n \log n + nm) for sorting and evaluation.

Uniform error bound: By Theorem 9.1, with probability 1 - \alpha,

\sup_j |\widehat{\Theta}_A(\lambda_j) - \Theta_A(\lambda_j)| \leq \sqrt{\frac{1}{2n} \log\left(\frac{2}{\alpha}\right)}.

