Appendix N — Glossary

Agent. A system A that produces actions in environments.

Acquisition time. \tau_A(T; \eta), the number of experience units required for A to reach competence \eta on task T.

Ambiguity set. \mathfrak{U}_\varepsilon(\mu), the set of measures within Wasserstein distance \varepsilon of \mu.

Autonomy axis. A function \mathcal{A} : \mathcal{T} \to \{0,1,2,3\} encoding the level of external support required.

Autonomy profile. \mathbf{A}_A = (A_0, A_1, A_2, A_3), where A_k = \mu(\mathcal{A} \geq k).

Collision audit. Systematic comparison of the proposed construction against prior art.

Composite task cost. c(T, T') = \alpha d_{\mathcal{X}} + \beta d_{\mathcal{Y}} + \gamma d_{\mathcal{R}}.

Dominance quantile. Q_A(\theta) = \Theta_A^{-1}(\theta).

Dominance region. \mathcal{D}_A = \{(\lambda, \theta) : \Theta_A(\lambda) \geq \theta\}.

Dominance survival function. \Theta_A(\lambda) = \mu(\{T : M_{A,H}^{(q)}(T) \geq \lambda\}).

Extended feasible region. \mathcal{F}_A \subseteq \mathbb{R}^5, the set of tuples satisfying all dominance conditions.

Generality. G_A = \Theta_A(0).

Human reference. p_H^{(q)}(T), the q-quantile of the human performance distribution on task T.

Logarithmic efficiency ratio. E_{A/H}(T; \eta) = \log((\tau_H + \delta) / (\tau_A + \delta)).

Margin. M_{A,H}^{(q)}(T) = p(A, T) - p_H^{(q)}(T).

Normalization axiom. Axiom N: normalization maps preserve quantile ordering and are monotone continuous.

Optimal-transport ambiguity. Robustness via Wasserstein balls.

Performance depth. P_A = \operatorname{ess\,sup}(X_A).

Product order. x \preceq y \iff x_i \leq y_i for all i.

Stochastic dominance. A \succeq_{\mathrm{SD}} B \iff \Theta_A(\lambda) \geq \Theta_B(\lambda) for all \lambda.

Structured task space. \mathfrak{T} = (\mathcal{T}, \tau_{\mathcal{T}}, \Sigma_{\mathcal{T}}, \mu).

Superhuman margin. M_{A,H}^{(q)}(T), the excess of A over the human reference quantile.

Task. T = (\mathcal{X}, \mathcal{Y}, \mathcal{E}, \mathcal{R}, \mathcal{C}, \tau, \nu).

